WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.560 --> 00:00:05.480
THE UNTOLD TRUTHS OF GOLD RUSH

00:00:05.480 --> 00:00:10.049
Viewers tune in season after season to watch
the cast of Gold Rush live out their modern

00:00:10.049 --> 00:00:15.240
day, forty-niner fantasies. But not everything
they do makes it to the airwaves. A little

00:00:15.240 --> 00:00:19.710
panning reveals that they take this outdated,
Old West profession and lifestyle of theirs

00:00:19.710 --> 00:00:25.150
way too seriously. Bring the canary in a cage,
because we're going into the mines to uncover

00:00:25.150 --> 00:00:27.269
the untold truths of Gold Rush.

00:00:27.269 --> 00:00:29.779
KILLIN' BEARS, WHO CARES

00:00:29.779 --> 00:00:35.790
The Gold Rush boys don't take kindly to any
varmint crossing their path, not even bears.

00:00:35.790 --> 00:00:40.100
According to the Associated Press, a bear
was needlessly killed during the show's production

00:00:40.100 --> 00:00:45.809
back in May 2010. The troubles began when
the bear stuck its nose in some untended graham

00:00:45.809 --> 00:00:50.420
crackers, and there's no worse crime in the
world than a bear sniffing at a man's crunchy

00:00:50.420 --> 00:00:55.940
sweets. Shortly thereafter, miner Mike Halstead
allegedly tracked the bear down and shot it

00:00:55.940 --> 00:01:01.039
dead. Though it was miles away from the mining
site...and probably wasn't actually the same

00:01:01.039 --> 00:01:04.839
bear...justice had been served. Kind of.

00:01:04.839 --> 00:01:06.360
SLAMMIN' THE SALMON

00:01:06.360 --> 00:01:10.860
The miners don't limit their war on the earth
to just bears. They make sure to take out

00:01:10.860 --> 00:01:15.760
some kind of wildlife in every way possible.
That's why they made sure to drive a 50-ton

00:01:15.760 --> 00:01:20.260
piece of heavy equipment through a salmon
habitat, according to a report from The Oregonian

00:01:20.260 --> 00:01:25.190
newspaper. According to the miners, state
laws allow them to drive their machinery through

00:01:25.190 --> 00:01:30.180
rivers and streams—it's just unfortunate
the fish got in their way. The fish were no

00:01:30.180 --> 00:01:35.540
match for the rig. By that tally, they've
killed one large land animal and a water animal

00:01:35.540 --> 00:01:40.090
habitat. Look out, birds: your days are numbered.

00:01:40.090 --> 00:01:42.120
THEY BASICALLY HATE NATURE

00:01:42.120 --> 00:01:47.090
The Gold Rush guys have also taken their war
on nature to the land itself. According to

00:01:47.090 --> 00:01:51.740
The Oregonian, they dug a trench to divert
the course of a stream, most likely to provide

00:01:51.740 --> 00:01:56.880
water for their camp. This is one clear violation
the gold rushers committed, as they failed

00:01:56.880 --> 00:02:01.650
to erect a screen to keep small fish from
swimming into the ditch. Thus, they not only

00:02:01.650 --> 00:02:06.160
increased their fish body count, but they
possibly did irreparable damage to the local

00:02:06.160 --> 00:02:10.679
ecosystem as well. Nice going, Team Gold.

00:02:10.679 --> 00:02:12.500
SLIMEY PRODUCERS

00:02:12.500 --> 00:02:15.900
With all the acts of aggression against the
Earth, of course the miners have been visited

00:02:15.900 --> 00:02:21.760
by state representatives. However, reps weren't
there to dole out citations. Instead, one

00:02:21.760 --> 00:02:26.819
rep showed the miners how to use ground water,
rather than diverting streams. That didn't

00:02:26.819 --> 00:02:31.930
sit well with the Discovery Channel's producers.
According to regional habitat supervisor Jackie

00:02:31.930 --> 00:02:36.709
Timothy, the producers actually wanted to
receive a fine. The resulting kerfuffle and

00:02:36.709 --> 00:02:40.959
media coverage would have provided the network
with some nice, discount publicity for the

00:02:40.959 --> 00:02:44.709
show. Too bad for them things went...well.

00:02:44.709 --> 00:02:46.209
PARKER SCHNABEL: MILLIONAIRE

00:02:46.209 --> 00:02:52.719
Though he pleads poverty on the show, Parker
Schnabel is actually filthy rich. In 2015,

00:02:52.719 --> 00:02:58.200
Fox News reported that Schnable earned himself
a million dollars during season five. A humble

00:02:58.200 --> 00:03:02.579
guy, he doesn't think people should be too
jealous of him. According to Schnabel, he's

00:03:02.579 --> 00:03:08.249
in more debt than anyone else his age, yet
he fails to supply any kind of numbers. Sounds

00:03:08.249 --> 00:03:10.760
like someone is hiding his gold...

00:03:10.760 --> 00:03:12.230
"DAKOTA" FRED SPLIT

00:03:12.230 --> 00:03:18.030
Mustachioed Gold Rush villain "Dakota" Fred
Hurt was a show fixture from seasons one through

00:03:18.030 --> 00:03:22.420
four. Then, he mysteriously up and left the
production and his co-workers, dragging his

00:03:22.420 --> 00:03:27.599
son with him. Some think he retreated to a
hermetic life in the mountains. Others believe

00:03:27.599 --> 00:03:32.249
he was raptured. What really happened is,
according to the Gazette Review, Hurt bought

00:03:32.249 --> 00:03:36.989
up all the Porcupine Creek land, where all
that sweet gold-digging action takes place,

00:03:36.989 --> 00:03:41.269
and told the Hoffmans and everyone else to
shove off. But really, that's not surprising

00:03:41.269 --> 00:03:44.779
behavior for a dude named "Hurt," is it?

00:03:44.779 --> 00:03:46.299
DAKOTA DEMANDED A RAISE

00:03:46.299 --> 00:03:51.069
In addition to thinking he'd find more success
on his own, Dakota Hurt also wanted more money

00:03:51.069 --> 00:03:56.209
from Discovery Channel. Hurt told the Gazette
Review that "if [the channel wants] him to

00:03:56.209 --> 00:04:00.489
be an actor, they need to give him the amount
of money an actor would get paid." Rather

00:04:00.489 --> 00:04:05.639
than accept Discovery's offer, Hurt went on
to film his own thing called All That Glitters.

00:04:05.639 --> 00:04:10.560
Whether it's a docu-series or a standalone
documentary isn't known, as no release information

00:04:10.560 --> 00:04:14.859
for All That Glitters has been announced as
of this video's production. Here's hoping

00:04:14.859 --> 00:04:16.970
Hurt made the right choice.

00:04:16.970 --> 00:04:18.810
JAMES HARNESS' FATAL ADDICTION

00:04:18.810 --> 00:04:23.850
Miner James Harness was a staple on Gold Rush
for the first two seasons before he was fired

00:04:23.850 --> 00:04:28.450
for missing the 100-ounce goal set by the
team. In his private life, Harness lived in

00:04:28.450 --> 00:04:33.700
constant pain, originally caused by a car
accident. That led to his addiction to painkillers,

00:04:33.700 --> 00:04:38.530
which in turn created Harness' problems on
the show. Unfortunately, his hardships didn't

00:04:38.530 --> 00:04:42.880
end once he was let go from the production.
Harness' addiction eventually resulted in

00:04:42.880 --> 00:04:47.840
the stroke that killed him in 2014, as reported
by TMZ.

00:04:47.840 --> 00:04:49.010
PARTS OF THE SHOW ARE SCRIPTED

00:04:49.010 --> 00:04:54.310
As with most reality shows, Gold Rush isn't
as real as promotions would have you believe.

00:04:54.310 --> 00:04:59.010
In an interview he gave to Oregon Gold, fired
miner Jimmy Dorsey claimed that parts of the

00:04:59.010 --> 00:05:04.000
show are scripted, and some surprising events
on the show are planned in advance. According

00:05:04.000 --> 00:05:08.260
to Dorsey, the Discovery Channel's producers
had scripted a fight between him and castmate

00:05:08.260 --> 00:05:13.140
Greg Remsburg, which would have resulted in
his exit from the show. In the process, Dorsey

00:05:13.140 --> 00:05:18.600
actually broke his ribs. He went on to say,
"They kind of push you towards making these

00:05:18.600 --> 00:05:20.230
things happen."

00:05:20.230 --> 00:05:22.250
TODD HOFFMAN HAS HIS DEMONS

00:05:22.250 --> 00:05:27.230
In the same interview, Dorsey also airs his
feelings about his former boss, Todd Hoffman.

00:05:27.230 --> 00:05:31.540
Saying he's a troubled man, Dorsey claims
Hoffman tossed aside friends and family in

00:05:31.540 --> 00:05:36.060
the pursuit of fame and fortune, even to the
point where he has no problem with others

00:05:36.060 --> 00:05:41.440
getting injured. Dorsey says that a particular
on-camera dressing down he received from Hoffman

00:05:41.440 --> 00:05:47.230
was not scripted at all. It was pure Hoffman.
He also went on to say Hoffman is uneducated

00:05:47.230 --> 00:05:52.140
in the ways of mining, but ultimately, Dorsey
feels sorry for Hoffman. At least he finally

00:05:52.140 --> 00:05:54.330
found something nice to say about him.

00:05:54.330 --> 00:05:58.410
Thanks for watching! Subscribe to our YouTube
channel to see more videos like the one you

00:05:58.410 --> 00:05:58.910
just saw.

